cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this publishing software, please cite it as below. To cite a research release published with it, use that release's own DOI instead."
title: "Evidence Press"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free static publishing system that turns research-release
  metadata and prose into a coordinated set of human-readable pages and
  machine-actionable scholarly objects: persistent identifiers, structured
  metadata, an explicit assurance matrix, evidence-package links, feeds,
  Signposting link sets, RO-Crate packaging and AI-provenance disclosure.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pitchford
    given-names: Ian
